<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar inflows at $84.8 mln June 4.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar inflows at $84.8 mln June 4.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $84.8 million surplus on June 4 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data suplied to banks.</p>
<p>The Central Bank corrected figures for June 3 to a $57.4 million deficit from a $412.8 million deficit. Dealers said the error occurred Tuesday when an import contract was registered with the wrong code for the foreign currency.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the Central Bank issued the following breakdown:</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON JUNE 3</p>
<p>Exports: $198.3 million</p>
<p>Imports: $253.9 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $265 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $266.8 million</p>
<p>Net deficit: $57.4 million</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON JUNE 4</p>
<p>Exports: $259.6 million</p>
<p>Imports: $228.3 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $362.2 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $308.7 million</p>
<p>Net surplus: $84.8 million</p>
<p>JUNE DOLLAR FLOWS UP DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $769.6 million</p>
<p>Imports: $788.6 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $951.6 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $851.8 million</p>
<p>Net surplus: $80.8 million</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>((--Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroon, 55 11 2485418))</p>
